# Release-profile nvcc flags for sm_89 (RTX 40 / Ada).
# One flag per line. Text from '#' to end of line is a comment; blank lines are
# ignored. Read by build_solver.{sh,bat} (release profile) and
# build_pool_miner.{sh,bat}. TARI_ARCH_FLAGS, when non-empty, replaces this list.
#
# Intentionally empty: a tuning sweep on real sm_89 hardware found no flag that
# beats the kernel defaults (including 50 trim rounds).
#
# Measured 2026-10-02 on NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4080 (16 GB, solver pipeline=2),
# driver 617.14, CUDA 13.4 (nvcc V13.4.59), MSVC VS 18 Build Tools, 340 W
# default power limit, clocks not locked.
# Benchmark: tari_c29_solver_sm_89.exe --count 2000 --nonce 0, 1 warm-up +
# 5 measured runs, median g/s. Keep rule: gain > 0.5% and > baseline spread.
#   baseline (no flags): 13.650 g/s (min 13.509, max 13.658, spread 1.09%)
#   final (no flags):    13.650 g/s, +0.00% (same set; drift re-runs of the
#                        baseline exe: 13.646, 13.634, 13.628, all within 0.16%)
#
# Tested alone on top of the empty set and rejected (RTX 4080, delta vs baseline):
#   ROUND23_TPB=768                                +0.02%  13.653  (neutral)
#   ROUND23_COUNT_NORMAL_LOAD=1                    -0.10%  13.637
#   ROUND1_COUNT_NORMAL_LOAD=1                     -0.12%  13.634
#   ROUND23_TPB=1024 (default, sanity check)       -0.17%  13.627
#   ROUND23_TPB=960                                -0.28%  13.612
#   ROUND_LATE_TPB=512                             -0.40%  13.596
#   ROUND0_DST_HASH group, BITS=11 PROBES=4        -0.53%  13.578
#   TARI_C29_DEFAULT_NTRIMS=48                     -0.76%  13.546
#   FUSE_FINAL_TAIL_CURRENT=1 + _COUNT_NORMAL_LOAD -0.86%  13.533
#   ROUND0_DST_HASH group, BITS=12 PROBES=8        -2.06%  13.369
#   ROUND0_DST_HASH group, BITS=12 PROBES=4        -3.90%  13.117
#   SEEDB_REVERSE_LOOP=1                           -4.69%  13.010
#   WARP_DST_ATOMICS_LATE=1                        -5.19%  12.942
#   ROUND_LATE_TPB=1024                            -6.64%  12.744
# (ROUND0_DST_HASH group = DYNAMIC_BITS/PROBES as listed plus FALLBACK_PLAIN=1,
# REPLAY_NORMAL_LOAD=1, REVERSE_INSERT=1.) No single flag helped, so there was
# nothing to combine. Several sm_120 (RTX 5090) flags are clear losses here.
